@startuml Trade Store Architecture

' Component Diagram with Kafka
title Trade Store - Event-Driven Architecture

package "Client Layer" {
  [API Client] as Client
}

package "API Layer (Write Path)" {
  [FastAPI Application] as API
  [Kafka Producer] as Producer
}

package "Message Queue" {
  queue "Apache Kafka" as Kafka {
    [Partition 0] as P0
    [Partition 1] as P1
    [Partition 2] as P2
  }
  [Zookeeper] as ZK
}

package "Consumer Layer" {
  [Kafka Consumer] as Consumer
  [Message Processor] as Processor
}

package "Business Logic Layer" {
  [TradeService] as Service
  [Validation Logic] as Validation
}

package "Data Access Layer" {
  [SQLAlchemy ORM] as ORM
  [Trade Model] as Model
}

package "Database Layer" {
  database "PostgreSQL" as DB {
    [trades table] as Table
  }
}

' Write Flow (Async)
Client --> API : POST/PUT/DELETE\n(HTTP)
API --> Producer : Build Message
Producer --> Kafka : Produce\n{operation, data}
Kafka --> Consumer : Poll Messages
Consumer --> Processor : Process Message
Processor --> Service : CRUD Operations
Service --> Validation : Validate Rules
Service --> ORM : Database Access
ORM --> Model : Map Objects
Model --> Table : Persist Data

' Read Flow (Sync)
Client --> API : GET (HTTP)
API --> Service : Query Data
Service --> ORM : Read Operations
ORM --> Table : SELECT
Table --> ORM : Result Set
ORM --> API : Trade Objects
API --> Client : JSON Response

' Kafka Infrastructure
Kafka --> ZK : Coordination
P0 --> Consumer : Consume
P1 --> Consumer : Consume
P2 --> Consumer : Consume

note right of Kafka
  **Topic:** trades
  **Partitions:** 3
  **Key:** trade_id
  **Replication:** 1 (dev)
  
  Ensures:
  - Ordering per trade
  - Parallel processing
  - Fault tolerance
end note

note right of Producer
  **Message Format:**
  {
    "operation": "CREATE|UPDATE|DELETE",
    "data": {trade_fields}
  }
end note

note right of Consumer
  **Processing:**
  - Manual offset commits
  - At-least-once delivery
  - Error handling with retry
  - Graceful shutdown
end note

note right of Validation
  **Multi-Layer:**
  1. Schema (Pydantic)
  2. Business Logic
  3. Database Constraints
end note

note left of Client
  **Write Operations:**
  Return 202 Accepted
  (Async via Kafka)
  
  **Read Operations:**
  Return 200 OK
  (Sync from DB)
end note

@enduml
